
## Research loop

- This project improves one number with `hi agent best-of` rounds
  (`make loop`). The number comes from a fixed evaluation: `evaluate.py`,
  `prepare.py`, and the data in `eval/`. During a run, agents change only the
  file `program.md` names; hi throws away results that change anything else.
- `eval/` is the frozen data the score is measured on. It is committed on
  purpose, unlike `data/`, so every box scores the same thing. Don't change
  it, the evaluation, or the metric in the middle of a run: scores before and
  after wouldn't compare.
- The holdout lives outside the repository, in `../<folder>-holdout/`. Never
  copy it in or read it from code; it is checked once, at the end, with
  `make holdout`.
- Boxes run offline from an image built from `uv.lock`. Don't add
  dependencies during a run; after a change to `uv.lock`, hi rebuilds the
  image on the next box.
- Run Python through `make` (`make score`, `make check`): it picks the box's
  environment in a box and uv's on this machine.
